Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `values` was consumed by a lambda that captures it, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/ownership/semantic_capture_events_drive_retention_and_deferred_clone_modes_3.jet:10:8
    |
 10 |     }, values)
    |        ^^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/ownership/semantic_capture_events_drive_retention_and_deferred_clone_modes_3.jet:9:21
    |
  9 |         #Reactive { values.push(3) }
    |                     ^^^^^^ `values` moved to a lambda that captures it here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `values` after the move, or give a lambda that captures it a copy with `values.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
